(footprint
  "Log-periodic_PCB_antenna__1-5_GHz"
  (at 100 100)
  (version 20221018)
  (generator pcb_antenna_designer)
  (layer "F.Cu")
  (descr "Log-periodic dipole array printed on a 205 x 160 mm FR-4 board (1.51 mm, epsilon r 4.6). A wideband, directional antenna. Simulated in a commercial EM tool: S11 below -10 dB in several bands from 1.6 to 4.7 GHz (for example -16.7 dB at 2.0 GHz, -14.4 dB at 2.4 GHz, -18.1 dB at 2.8 GHz, -18.6 dB at 4.6 GHz), with peaks of -4 to -8 dB between them. Those results come from a run with a 0.25 mm mesh on the copper (22.6 M cells). The template uses 0.8 mm (3.2 M cells, λ/40 in the substrate at 5 GHz) so it runs in a reasonable time; checked on the GPU: the same bands within a few dB (152 of 401 points below -10 dB from 1.94 to 4.66 GHz, -18.8 dB at 3.2 GHz, -17.8 dB at 3.8 GHz), and at 3.0 GHz directivity 5.6 dBi, radiation efficiency 47 %, peak gain 2.3 dBi. Set Fine mesh on metal back to 0.25 mm for the final check.")
  (tags "antenna IFA MIFA RF")
